  "title": "Nearly spanning regular subgraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every $\\epsilon > 0$ and every positive integer $k$, there exists $r_0 = r_0(\\epsilon,k)$ so that every simple $r$-regular graph $G$ with $r \\ge r_0$ has a $k$-regular subgraph $H$ with $|V(H)| \\ge (1- \\epsilon) |V(G)|$.",
